{"title":"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A drawer in a darkened room contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> red socks, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> green socks, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> blue socks and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> black socks. \nA youngster selects socks one at a time from the drawer but is unable to see the color of the socks drawn. \nWhat is the smallest number of socks that must be selected to guarantee that the selection contains at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pairs? \n(A pair of socks is two socks of the same color. No sock may be counted in more than one pair.)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1d89e18dcad0bde6e5b30cbd489cbc78c5ec80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 21\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 23\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 24\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 30\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>~ e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p><br />\nSuppose that you wish to draw one pair of socks from the drawer. Then you would pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> socks (one of each kind, plus one). Notice that in the worst possible situation, you will continue to draw the same sock, until you get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pairs. This is because drawing the same sock results in a pair every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of that sock, whereas drawing another sock creates another pair. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca2cfc3a07fc15596e6d0ba3738e2ba069d922c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+2\\cdot(10-1) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"206\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>~ Levieee (formatted shalomkeshet)\n</p><p>We have to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f3d89d19ce499163041966ac9101e97c3bee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> of socks, i.e <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> socks\n</p><p>We choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> socks in the worst possible scenario there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f3d89d19ce499163041966ac9101e97c3bee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> socks that are not paired, so we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more socks to this, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> can be the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d23026745bf786359d9957bc252d79f05b9f27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$odd$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37214fbfecdee24d74c3fe6888304d43ed4ddb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$numbers$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" /> (like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6200bcd68a26013998c00cd54ee22a04fcfde21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,7,7,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />)\n</p><p>This means there might be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f3d89d19ce499163041966ac9101e97c3bee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and a few unpaired. If we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, it cannot be formed by summing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d23026745bf786359d9957bc252d79f05b9f27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$odd$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37214fbfecdee24d74c3fe6888304d43ed4ddb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$numbers$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f3d89d19ce499163041966ac9101e97c3bee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> of socks in it. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cannot happen because in the worst case scenario, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f3d89d19ce499163041966ac9101e97c3bee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a47b00891750d85e15cadb945324b8dc7e206ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$unpaired$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />, then pulling out one more will leave us with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f3d89d19ce499163041966ac9101e97c3bee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />. However, the question demands <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/7504e4155d13891480cc48c5285047532bc39c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 pairs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> cannot happen either because if we pull out another sock it can be the same colour as the one we pulled out before, meaning it cannot be paired, but if we pull out another one and in the worst case scenario if the colour is same it still forms a pair with the last sock that we pulled out, therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c33498e668949cf220e6a9007774865996de945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> colors of socks, any selected set of socks could contain at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> unpaired socks.  So a set of socks which contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or fewer matched pairs could have at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a0182d9d8e04a77fd8ecfc7217c5e354a240b5a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 2 \\cdot 9 = 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> socks.  This could happen if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> red socks and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sock of each other color are selected.  So the minimum number of socks needed to guarantee <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> matched pairs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/605b588490cd0b041ee9b974297350de7d14456f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of red, green, blue, and black socks selected, respectively.  Then the number of matched pairs of socks is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1596a10a3dd46f01129b9ca58fd60e4ac5edde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{w}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{x}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{y}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{z}{2} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"202\" height=\"35\" />.  Note that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba4c4b2367961d298e5e7d0ec48ecee37fc4ff8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor = \\frac{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"35\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/1/9712d0309e86a9a1662109d4a8618b87fd52f953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor = \\frac{n-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474aa34542a920d5ae7b3f373de00cf09fae5e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{w}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{x}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{y}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{z}{2} \\right\\rfloor \\geq \\frac{w-1}{2} + \\frac{x-1}{2} + \\frac{y-1}{2} + \\frac{z-1}{2} = \\frac{w+x+y+z}{2} - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"646\" height=\"38\" />.  Thus if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/35865ca5b62bea76fa92b9120a8c3c370e23e027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor \\frac{w}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{x}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{y}{2} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\frac{z}{2} \\right\\rfloor \\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"236\" height=\"35\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/8483340642ec6c9ee2598d1a1b44a4dec1afdc3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w+x+y+z}{2} - 2 \\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"180\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27ceddb811b5857a4a383965090598323534bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w+x+y+z \\leq 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"17\" />.  That is, a set of socks containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or fewer matched pairs contains at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> socks.  Several equality cases exist, such as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53ec77d0412ea576f9b24f5b4345d103dd05f6db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(w, x, y, z) = (19, 1, 1, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" />.  So the minimum number of socks needed to guarantee <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> matched pairs is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/5/605b588490cd0b041ee9b974297350de7d14456f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22 + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"140\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You want to maximize the amount of odd numbers of socks you get. One way you can do this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/5506e92ec4425ca9359a8d3fffee5241ce871db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,1,1,21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"17\" /> socks to give you 10 pairs. However, you would not be able to get the last sock, giving you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66dd4d5902c2ab7fb10d7ef9971cfbcb6d6d1b99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1+1+20=23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" /> socks.\n-megacleverstarfish15\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME\" title=\"1986 AHSME\">1986 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-a